#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:1
msgid "Release 1.10 (2015-09-03)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. It also has a number of new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:6
msgid ""
"A number of builtin functions have been added to reduce Nixpkgs/NixOS "
"evaluation time and memory consumption: `all`, `any`, `concatStringsSep`, "
"`foldl’`, `genList`, `replaceStrings`, `sort`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:10
msgid "The garbage collector is more robust when the disk is full."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:12
msgid ""
"Nix supports a new API for building derivations that doesn’t require a `."
"drv` file to be present on disk; it only requires an in-memory "
"representation of the derivation. This is used by the Hydra continuous build "
"system to make remote builds more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:17
msgid ""
"The function `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now uses a _builtin_ builder (i.e. it "
"doesn’t require starting an external process; the download is performed by "
"Nix itself). This ensures that derivation paths don’t change when Nix is "
"upgraded, and obviates the need for ugly hacks to support chroot execution."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:23
msgid ""
"`--version -v` now prints some configuration information, in particular what "
"compile-time optional features are enabled, and the paths of various "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:27
msgid "Build users have their supplementary groups set correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:29
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Eelco Dolstra, Guillaume Maudoux, Iwan "
"Aucamp, Jaka Hudoklin, Kirill Elagin, Ludovic Courtès, Manolis Ragkousis, "
"Nicolas B. Pierron and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""
